   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Futures with an irregular stem",
     "texto": [
      "The future is used to **predict** (**Mañana lloverá**), to **promise** (**Te llamaré**) and to talk about what **will happen**. Twelve very common verbs change their stem, but the endings are the usual ones.\n\nFor a plan that is already decided, **ir a + infinitive** is very common: **Voy a comprar** un coche.\n\nWith **dentro de** you count time from now: **dentro de dos años**.\n\nAnd be careful with **si**: a real condition takes the present, not the future."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Irregular future stems",
     "texto": [
      "The endings are the same for every verb: **-é, -ás, -á, -emos, -éis, -án**. What changes is the stem:\n\n- They lose a vowel: poder → **podr**é, saber → **sabr**é, querer → **querr**é, haber → **habr**á, caber → **cabr**é.\n- They gain a **d**: tener → **tendr**é, venir → **vendr**é, poner → **pondr**é, salir → **saldr**é, valer → **valdr**é.\n- They shorten: hacer → **har**é, decir → **dir**é.\n\nWith **si** + present the condition is real: **Si ahorro**, **podré** comprar una casa. After **si** the future is not used."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
